      "writtenOn": "2021-10-19T16:55:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Valid points. Want to see other\u0027s opinions.\n\nIMO, complex code can be simplified by better software architecture, like abstraction, code refactoring, etc. We don\u0027t need to preserve original code structure, which implements all functions in a single big file. The important thing is the easy-understandable dt definition. The partners just need to modify the dt file.\n\nThis CL is just a beginning, still far away from the final destination. Parth chose to use an incremental and iterative approach, starting from the Lazor\u0027s LED policy, and step-by-step to extend to more boards. So this CL may not be fit other boards\u0027 policies; just try to make the dt node general enough so won\u0027t be super pain to extend to other boards in the future.",
      "parentUuid": "9b857393_276cfbef",
      "revId": "63e7af6d2c0b21be8e972d64fd30eb8641672e61",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
